  {%- when 'condition_tab_1' -%}
    {%- case page.handle -%}
      {%- when 'anti-aging' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Skin ageing: everyday care and responsible next steps</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Skin changes with age, and sun exposure can contribute to premature ageing.</p>

          <h2>Everyday care</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Protect your skin from the sun each day.</li>
            <li>Cleanse gently instead of scrubbing.</li>
            <li>Moisturise when the skin feels dry or tight.</li>
            <li>Use each product exactly as its label directs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>No topical product can promise to reverse ageing or solve every skin concern.</p>

          <h2>When to seek advice</h2>
          <p>For questions about a skin change, ask a doctor or dermatologist.</p>

          <h2>Choose with the label in front of you</h2>
          <p>Compare the exact product's ingredients, directions and warnings before deciding whether it suits your routine. This guide does not recommend a product or treatment.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Browse products</a><a href="/pages/product-faqs">Product FAQs</a><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/anti-aging/reduce-premature-aging-skin" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">American Academy of Dermatology, premature skin ageing guidance</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'arthritis' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Arthritis: symptoms and next steps</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Arthritis can cause pain, swelling and stiffness in one or more joints.</p>

          <h2>Get urgent medical care if</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>A joint becomes suddenly hot, red or very swollen.</li>
            <li>You feel generally unwell with the joint symptoms.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>If symptoms are persistent</h2>
          <p>Arrange a medical assessment for unexplained joint pain, swelling or stiffness that persists.</p>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not recommend a product, dose or course of treatment for arthritis.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/product-faqs">Product FAQs</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/arthritis/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Arthritis</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'slipped-disc' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Slipped disc: symptoms and emergency signs</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">A slipped or herniated disc happens when tissue between the bones of the spine bulges outward. It may press on nearby nerves.</p>

          <h2>Go to hospital immediately if</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>You lose bladder or bowel control, or cannot pass urine.</li>
            <li>You develop numbness around the genitals, buttocks or inner thighs.</li>
            <li>You develop major or worsening weakness in the legs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These signs can mean serious pressure on spinal nerves and need emergency assessment.</p>

          <h2>If it is not an emergency</h2>
          <p>Arrange a medical assessment if symptoms persist, worsen or worry you.</p>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not claim that an Ayurvedic product can move a disc into place or cure a slipped disc. Get a diagnosis before considering supportive care.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/slipped-disc/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Slipped disc</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'cataract' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Cataracts: symptoms and eye checks</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">A cataract is clouding of the lens inside the eye. It can cause gradual blurred vision, glare, poorer night vision or colours that look faded.</p>

          <h2>What to do</h2>
          <p>Arrange an examination with an eye professional. An examination can identify the cause of a vision change and help you discuss whether treatment is needed. Surgery is the established corrective treatment for cataracts when needed.</p>

          <h2>Use professional eye advice</h2>
          <p>Use only eye treatments advised by a qualified eye professional. This page does not provide a home eye-wash, purging or dosing routine.</p>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not recommend a Kairali product or home procedure for cataracts.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a><a href="/pages/product-faqs">Product FAQs</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/cataracts/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Cataracts in adults</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'dark-circles' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Dark circles under the eyes</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Dark circles are a visible concern rather than one diagnosis. Fatigue can contribute, but appearance alone does not show the cause.</p>

          <h2>What may contribute</h2>
          <p>Fatigue can contribute to the appearance of dark circles, but the appearance alone does not establish a cause.</p>

          <h2>When to have the change assessed</h2>
          <p>Seek professional advice if the change is persistent, appears on one side, or comes with pain, swelling or a change in vision.</p>

          <h2>Choose responsibly</h2>
          <p>This guide does not diagnose the cause or recommend a product as a treatment for dark circles. Compare ingredients, directions and warnings before choosing facial care.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Browse products</a><a href="/pages/product-faqs">Product FAQs</a><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">General information bounded by the governed Kairali India source review. It does not replace advice from a qualified professional.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'facial-paralysis' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Sudden facial weakness: get emergency help</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Sudden weakness or drooping on one side of the face can be a sign of stroke. Treat it as an emergency until a qualified professional says otherwise.</p>

          <h2>Call local emergency services now if</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>One side of the face has dropped or the person cannot smile evenly.</li>
            <li>One arm is weak or cannot be raised and held up.</li>
            <li>Speech is slurred, confused or absent.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Any one of these signs needs immediate assessment. Do not wait for it to pass.</p>

          <h2>If stroke has been ruled out</h2>
          <p>Bell's palsy is another possible cause of one-sided facial weakness and also needs prompt professional assessment.</p>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>Do not delay emergency assessment to try an oil, tablet, nasal preparation or massage routine. This guide does not recommend a product or regimen for facial paralysis.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India for a non-urgent product question</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/bells-palsy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Bell's palsy</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'heart-diseases' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Heart and blood vessel disease: warning signs</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Cardiovascular disease is a general term for disorders of the heart and blood vessels.</p>

          <h2>Get urgent medical help for</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Chest pain, pressure or discomfort</li>
            <li>Sudden difficulty breathing or faintness</li>
            <li>Sudden weakness on one side of the face or body</li>
            <li>Sudden slurred or confused speech</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These signs need urgent assessment. Contact local emergency services and do not wait for them to pass.</p>

          <h2>If you are concerned but it is not an emergency</h2>
          <p>Arrange a medical assessment rather than relying on a retail page for diagnosis.</p>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not recommend a remedy or dose for heart disease.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India for a non-urgent product question</a><a href="/pages/quality-and-safety">Quality and safety</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/cardiovascular-diseases-%28cvds%29" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">World Health Organization, cardiovascular diseases</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'hemorrhoids' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Piles (haemorrhoids): symptoms and when to get help</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Piles, also called haemorrhoids, are swollen blood vessels or lumps in or around the anus.</p>

          <h2>Do not self-diagnose bleeding</h2>
          <p>Rectal bleeding can have causes other than piles. Arrange medical advice rather than assuming the cause.</p>

          <h2>Get medical care promptly if</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Bleeding is severe, persistent or will not stop.</li>
            <li>You have severe pain.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not recommend a product or dose for piles. Discuss bleeding and persistent symptoms with a qualified health professional before considering supportive care.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/online-consultation">Online consultation information</a><a href="/pages/product-faqs">Product FAQs</a><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/piles-haemorrhoids/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Piles (haemorrhoids)</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'hypertension' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>High blood pressure: why measurement matters</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">High blood pressure, or hypertension, commonly causes no symptoms. Measuring blood pressure is the way to detect it.</p>

          <h2>Get your blood pressure checked</h2>
          <p>Ask a qualified health professional to measure it and explain what the reading means for you. Do not judge your blood pressure only by how you feel.</p>

          <h2>Get immediate medical care if</h2>
          <p>A very high reading comes with chest pain, difficulty breathing, confusion or a change in vision.</p>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not recommend an Ayurvedic product, oil or dose for high blood pressure. Follow the treatment plan given by your qualified health professional.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India for a non-urgent product question</a><a href="/pages/quality-and-safety">Quality and safety</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/hypertension" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">World Health Organization, hypertension</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>

      {%- when 'liver-diseases' -%}
        <article class="in037-b02 in037-b02--guide">
          <h1>Liver disease: signs and getting checked</h1>
          <p class="in037-b02__lead">Many liver diseases can have no early symptoms. A suspected liver problem needs medical assessment rather than self-treatment.</p>

          <h2>Signs to have assessed</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Yellowing of the skin or whites of the eyes (jaundice)</li>
            <li>Persistent weakness or tiredness</li>
            <li>Loss of appetite</li>
            <li>Persistent itching</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>About Kairali products</h2>
          <p>This guide does not claim that a Kairali product protects the liver, prevents damage, restores liver function or neutralises toxins.</p>
          <p class="in037-b02__actions"><a href="/pages/contact-us">Contact Kairali India for a non-urgent product question</a><a href="/pages/quality-and-safety">Quality and safety</a></p>

          <p class="in037-b02__source">Source: <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/liver-disease/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS, Liver disease</a>. General information only.</p>
        </article>
